    <text>
        <body>
            <div xml:id="d442">

                <pb facs="0459" n="361" xml:id="pg361"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">711.933/244: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Consul General at Canton</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic">Jenkins</hi>) <hi
                        rendition="#italic">to the Acting Secretary of
                            State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Canton</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1930-01-13T12:00:00+08:00">January 13,
                        1930—noon</date>.<lb/>[Received January 13—6 a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to the Legation’s telegram January 8, 10 a.m.,<anchor n="49"
                        xml:id="d442-f1"/> I visited informally Mayor of Canton on January 11 when I
                    took occasion to assure him of cooperation of American Consulate General and
                    discussed several pending matters. Mayor has arranged to return visit today.
                    Other Consuls are pursuing similar course, and relations now seem well
                    established. Department and Legation informed.</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Jenkins</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
    </text>
    <standOff>
        <listAnnotation>
            <note corresp="#d442-f1" n="49" xml:id="d442-f1-content">
                <p>Copy apparently not received in the Department; see Department’s telegram No. 6,
                    January 6, to the Chargé in China, <ref target="#pg360">p. 360</ref>.</p>
            </note>
        </listAnnotation>
    </standOff>
